    {
      "argv": [
        "node",
        "/Users/brad/.cache/swarm-comparison/tools/swarm-736251101/dist/cli.js",
        "When mocha must start a second Node process (a Node or V8 flag such as --enable-source-maps was given, or --node-option was used), bin/mocha.js turns the options it loaded back into command-line arguments with unparseMochaArgs from lib/cli/unparse-args.js and passes them to the child. Today an option with a scalar value is emitted as two arguments, the flag and then the value (unparseMochaArgs({ reporter: \"json\" }) gives [\"--reporter\", \"json\"]), except dotted names such as reporter-option.foo, which are emitted as one \"--name=value\" argument. An option the child has no definition for is then read as a boolean flag and its value as a test file: in a directory whose .mocharc.json holds \"$schema\": \"https://json.schemastore.org/mocharc.json\" and \"spec\": \"a.spec.cjs\", running mocha --enable-source-maps prints Warning: Cannot find any files matching pattern \"https://json.schemastore.org/mocharc.json\" before running a.spec.cjs (without the Node flag no child is started and there is no warning). Emit every option that carries a value as one \"--name=value\" argument, whatever its name: unparseMochaArgs({ $schema: \"https://json.schemastore.org/mocharc.json\" }) must give [\"--$schema=https://json.schemastore.org/mocharc.json\"]; unparseMochaArgs({ _: [\"test/a.spec.js\"], reporter: \"json\" }) must give [\"test/a.spec.js\", \"--reporter=json\"]; unparseMochaArgs({ require: [\"tsx\", \"./setup.js\"], timeout: \"0\" }) must give [\"--require=tsx\", \"--require=./setup.js\", \"--timeout=0\"]; unparseMochaArgs({ slow: 75 }) must give [\"--slow=75\"]; unparseMochaArgs({ grep: \"--x\" }) must give [\"--grep=--x\"]. What must not change: positionals come first; true gives \"--name\", false gives \"--no-name\", null and undefined give nothing (unparseMochaArgs({ bail: true, color: false, ui: null }) gives [\"--bail\", \"--no-color\"]); an array repeats the option once per item; an object value is flattened into dotted names (unparseMochaArgs({ \"reporter-option\": { foo: \"bar\", baz: true } }) still gives [\"--reporter-option.foo=bar\", \"--reporter-option.baz\"]); and unparseNodeFlags, which already writes \"--name=value\", is unchanged. Some existing cases in test/node-unit/cli/unparse-args.spec.js expect the two-argument form; they describe the behaviour being replaced, so update their expected arguments to the one-argument form without removing any case. Add regression tests for this behaviour to the project's existing test suite. The unit tests run with npm run test-node:unit (mocha under nyc over test/unit and test/node-unit).\n\nVisible acceptance check (it must pass; it is not the only criterion): node acceptance/visible/check.mjs\nThe project's own tests run with: npm run test-node:unit\nDeliverables, all required; the task is not done until each is in the tree:\n1. The implementation of the behaviour described above, in the project's own source.\n2. Regression tests: at least one new test case, in the project's own test directory and style, that fails on the current code and passes with your change, adding at least one new assertion. A change without a new test is incomplete.\n3. The visible acceptance check (node acceptance/visible/check.mjs) and the project's own test command (npm run test-node:unit) both passing on the final tree.\nAllowed changes: implementation code, and regression tests for the change (new test files, or new cases added to existing test files, in the project's own test directory and style).\nDo not modify anything under acceptance/visible/.\nDo not change how the project's checks run: leave the test and coverage configuration files (.taprc*, .nycrc*, .c8rc*, .mocharc*, jest.config.*, vitest.config.*, ava.config.*, karma.conf.*) and the test, pretest and posttest scripts and runner sections of package.json as they are.\nDo not delete or weaken existing tests: keep every existing assertion (it may move to another test file), add no skip, only or todo markers, and add no coverage-ignore pragmas. A change that does any of these is rejected at evaluation whatever else passes.",
